  "guide": [
    {
      "title": "Lighting",
      "icon": "on",
      "text": "Use Lights on and Lights off on Home for everyday lighting.\n\nRoom tools → Lighting brings White light, Scenes, Programmes and Channels together. Opening a tab does not change the lights.\n\nA highlighted button shows the last confirmed setting. If a result is uncertain, stop and ask the room host."
    },
    {
      "title": "Room controls",
      "icon": "home",
      "text": "Home always returns to everyday lighting controls. Opening a page does not change the lights.\n\nLegacy opens the original interface after restoring Beta’s starting lighting scene. Use Home in the Legacy bar to return.\n\nLift blinds, Open slats and Close & lower are on Home. Room tools → Screen & controls saves whether blind movement is enabled and whether the controls are shown. Movement is disabled by default and also requires a connected controller."
    },
    {
      "title": "Sensors and experiments",
      "icon": "experiment",
      "text": "Experiment mode guides a repeatable sequence of instructions and saves panel annotations.\n\nIt does not start a recorder. Arrange recording separately and coordinate the study with the room host.\n\nRoom tools → System & help shows room service availability. Availability alone does not prove usable sensor data."
    },
    {
      "title": "How it connects",
      "icon": "health",
      "text": "The touch panel and trusted-network website share Beta controls. Legacy’s original controls remain on the touch panel.\n\nThe lighting badge shows this panel’s connection: Ready, Sending, Offline or Uncertain. Tap it for System & help.\n\nWeather is an outdoor model estimate, separate from indoor measurements. Source details are under Room tools → Date & weather."
    }
  ],
  "help": [
    {
      "title": "Lighting",
      "text": "Ready means the lighting adapter is available. Sending means a request is awaiting readback.\n\nIf Uncertain appears, stop changing lights and ask the room host. A failed response can leave the result unknown.\n\nIf Offline appears, check the panel network cable and the room computer. Legacy also needs the room services.",
      "commands": "",
      "command_tokens": []
    },
    {
      "title": "Power",
      "text": "An undervoltage warning means the Pi supply voltage is too low. This can slow the panel and affect storage reliability.\n\nCheck the supply, cable and connector. A separately powered LCD does not rule out a Pi power problem.\n\nDo not hide the warning or keep power-cycling to clear it. Shut down normally before changing power.",
      "commands": "vcgencmd get_throttled",
      "command_tokens": [
        {
          "text": "vcgencmd",
          "kind": "command"
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "get_throttled",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Ubuntu checks",
      "text": "Use a Terminal on the Ubuntu room computer. These commands inspect state; they do not start devices.\n\nROS owns room controls. Status owns the TV display and its clients. Session presence alone does not prove health.",
      "commands": "hostname\nuptime\nfree -m\ndf -h /\ntmux list-sessions\nsource /opt/ros/indigo/setup.bash\nsource ~/catkin_ws/devel/setup.bash\ntimeout 10 rosservice list",
